  "label": "She Never Thought She Would Lose, Until She Did",
  "description": "This phrase is a narrative trope often used to describe a situation where someone who was perceived as invincible or unbeatable suffers a humiliating defeat. In the context of the meme, it implies a narrative of betrayal and downfall, further fueling resentment and a desire for retribution. This phrase is commonly used in political and social commentary to frame a loss as a moral or existential catastrophe.",
